  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 401 AM EST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nLong range models depict a synoptic scenario with a series of \nshortwave troughs aloft passing through the area late this week and \ninto the weekend, while some drier air filters into the mid/low \nlvls. Meanwhile, model consensus is increasing regarding the \npotential for a dry frontal passage for the later part of the work \nweek. \n\nThere is also a potential shortwave cutting off from the northern \nstream and slowly moving across the E CONUS, which will ultimately \ndecide when/if we get the FROPA all the way into SoFlo later this\nweek. Regardless of the final outcome, models still keep this \nFROPA fairly dry with little indications of significant \nrain/thunderstorm activity associated with it. Winds are also \nexpected to diminish as pressure gradients relax in the wake of \nthe frontal passage. \n\nTemperatures will generally remain in the mid to upper 80s,\nwarmest over southern areas of SoFlo.",
